[Music]  the european parliament welcomes the 750  billion euro covid 19 recovery fund  agreed by eu leaders  but says it must not come at the cost of  the eu's long-term budget priorities  i'm not happy about the deal  we think that it is not giving proper  answers to the challenges of the next  seven years  it has to be more future orientated  to ensure a sustainable long-term  recovery parliament says investment in  the green deal  the digital economy erasmus health and  research  must be safeguarded it says cuts to  flagship eu programs  are unacceptable  insist that parliament will not give its  consent without an agreement on the  introduction of new  eu revenue sources such as a levy on  non-recycled plastic waste  or on co2 emissions which would help  cover the cost of the recovery plan  the european parliament is also  concerned that eu leaders weakened  efforts to include protections to the  rule of law by limiting eu funding to  countries failing to uphold media  freedoms and human rights  parliament wants negotiations to  conclude by the end of october  for a smooth start to eu programmes from  [Music]  2021

